# NOT needed for a normal install.
#
# The plugin talks to BrowserStack's hosted MCP server over HTTP and the client signs
# you in by OAuth — see .mcp.json / .cursor-mcp.json / codex-mcp.example.toml. Nothing
# below is read on that route, and there is no .env to create.
#
# These exist only for the LOCAL FALLBACK: running @browserstack/mcp-server yourself
# over stdio, which is the commented block at the bottom of codex-mcp.example.toml.
# That route needs credentials because it is your machine talking to the API directly.
#
# Per-user. Never commit real values — .env is gitignored, this example file is not.
BROWSERSTACK_USERNAME=
BROWSERSTACK_ACCESS_KEY=
